{number: 148}
{title: Yesterday, Today, Forever}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Oh, [Ab] how sweet the glorious message
Simple [Db] faith may [Ab] claim;
Yesterday, today, forever,
[Eb7] Jesus is the [Ab] same!
Still He loves to save the sinful,
Heal the [Db] sick and [Ab] lame,
Cheer the mourner, still the tempest.
[Eb7] Glory to His [Ab] name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Ab] Yesterday, today, forever,
[Db] Jesus is the [Ab] same.
All may change, but Jesus never!
Glory to His [Eb7] name!
[Ab] Glory to His [Db] name!
[Ab] Glory to His [Eb7] name!
All may change, but Jesus [Ab] never!
Glory to His [Eb7] [Ab] name!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Him [Ab] who pardon'd erring Peter,
Never [Db] need'st thou [Ab] fear;
He that came to faithless Thomas,
[Eb7] All thy doubt will [Ab] clear.
He who let the lov'd disciple
On His [Db] bosom [Ab] rest
Bids thee still, with love as tender,
[Eb7] Lean upon His [Ab] breast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
He [Ab] who mid the raging billows
Walk'd up-[Db] on the [Ab] sea
Still can hush our wildest tempest,
[Eb7] As on Gali-[Ab] lee
He who wept and pray'd in anguish,
In Geth-[Db] sema-[Ab] ne,
Drinks with us each cup of trembling,
[Eb7] In our ago-[Ab] ny.
{end_of_verse}
